# Getting Ready for Unit 4

<img src="https://images.code.org/9ab6ee4aa2b383e62554584bc9011253-MS18.png" alt="Insert alt text here" style="width: 30%; border-radius: 10px; margin: 0px 0px 10px 10px; float: right;">

This professional learning module is designed to give you a guided preview of the **key concepts, coding practices, and instructional approaches** students will encounter in Unit 4.

In this unit, students move from writing code that works with one piece of information at a time to using **loops** to process entire collections of data. They also explore how filtering decisions shape what users see, what gets left out, and how much trust users can place in an app.

As you move through this module, focus on how students build both technical confidence and critical awareness. You’ll consider how to support students as they implement loops, create filters and searches, evaluate algorithmic transparency, and make intentional decisions about when to adapt, write, or refactor code.

<br>

## This Module Covers:

<div style="width: 100%; margin: 25px 0px;">

<div style="display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 15px; margin-bottom: 15px;">

<div style="background-color: #F5F7F8; color: #000000; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; width: 30%; min-height: 180px; text-align: center; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); box-sizing: border-box;">
      <p style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">🔁 Introducing Loops</p>
      <p style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.3; margin: 0;">
        Explore how repeated logic helps programs process collections of data instead of single items.
      </p>
    </div>

  <div style="background-color: #F5F7F8; color: #000000; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; width: 30%; min-height: 180px; text-align: center; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); box-sizing: border-box;">
    <p style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">🔎 Filtering and Transparency</p>
      <p style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.3; margin: 0;">
        Consider how filtering choices affect fairness, inclusivity, transparency, and user trust.
      </p>
    </div>

<div style="background-color: #F5F7F8; color: #000000; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; width: 30%; min-height: 180px; text-align: center; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); box-sizing: border-box;">
      <p style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">📋 Copying Data</p>
      <p style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.3; margin: 0;">
        Learn how students use data structures thoughtfully as they prepare information for searching, filtering, and display.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>

  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 15px;">

<div style="background-color: #F5F7F8; color: #000000; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; width: 30%; min-height: 180px; text-align: center; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); box-sizing: border-box;">
  <p style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">🧮 Filtering Data</p>
    <p style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.3; margin: 0;">
        Practice using loops in JavaScript to build interactive features such as filters, searches, and views.
      </p>
    </div>

<div style="background-color: #F5F7F8; color: #000000; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; width: 30%; min-height: 180px; text-align: center; box-shadow: 2px 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); box-sizing: border-box;">
      <p style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 10px;">🤖 AI Pedagogy Support</p>
      <p style="font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.3; margin: 0;">
        Explore how to help students document, justify, and take ownership of coding decisions when using AI support.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>

</div>

---

As you move through the module, focus on building confidence with loops and filtering, noticing opportunities for student reasoning, and making connections to how students can create more transparent and trustworthy data-driven apps.
